    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d587">

                <pb facs="0604" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg594"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/11–2849</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Chinese
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sprouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-11-28">November 28, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Reference is made to your memorandum of November 18, 1949 requesting information
                    which could be transmitted to Mr. Graves concerning the present status of the
                    $125 Million Grants to China. Mr. Yost (FE) obtained from U.S. Government
                    agencies a report on the status of materials yet to be transferred by those
                    agencies under the Grants. In order to check on shipments of military materiel
                    purchased by the Chinese Government through commercial sources CA requested the
                    Munitions Division to provide data on approved but as yet unused export licenses
                    covering such shipments. The data provided by the Munitions Division includes
                    shipments of materiel procured commercially under the $125 million program. A
                    consolidated picture of significant items which remain to be shipped, derived
                    from the reports of Mr. Yost and the Munitions Division, is provided in the
                    attached memorandum which may be handed to Mr. Graves.</p>


                <xi:include href="d587-a1.xml" xpointer="d587-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
